1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,000
[roars]

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,000
[narrator] Strange beasts

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,000
and monsters.

4
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Vast riches.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Hidden treasures.

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Evil haunts.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Uncharted frontiers.

8
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
The mysterious unknown.

9
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,000
The people who are captivated
by the magic in those words…

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:27,000
are called…

11
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Hunters.

12
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,000
[theme song playing]

13
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:54,000
[Gon] Leorio!

14
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:56,000
[both gasp]

15
00:01:58,000 --> 00:01:59,000
[grimacing in pain]

16
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,000
[Gon] Leorio!

17
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:09,000
BIG x TIME x INTERVIEW

18
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:16,000
[narrator] Gon and his group
have been trapped by vipers,

19
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:18,000
which now block their exit.

20
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:21,000
But the vipers’ master, Bourbon...

21
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,000
is dead.

22
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:27,000
Are you telling us that the person
who set this trap is now dead?

23
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:28,000
But how?

24
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Well, I killed him.

25
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,000
But my methods are a trade secret.

26
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Hey, Gon. Take Leorio.

27
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,000
[gasp]

28
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,000
[Ponzu] It’s no use.

29
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:01,000
I’m sorry,
but you won’t be able to search him.

30
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,000
The snakes are trained.

31
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:05,000
And if you even try to touch him

32
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,000
or you try to leave the cave and escape,

33
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,000
every single one of them will attack you.

34
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:18,000
[Kurapika]
So, you fought poison with poison.

35
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Judging by his wounds,
you must have used Neurotoxic Bees.

36
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:25,000
So, it’s likely that he died
of anaphylactic shock.

37
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:27,000
“Anaphylactic”?

38
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,000
What is that?

39
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,000
When a bee stings a human,

40
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:33,000
certain antibodies are produced

41
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:36,000
in an attempt to counter the effects
of the bee’s venom.

42
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:39,000
But if that person is stung again

43
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,000
by the same kind of bee,

44
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
they will experience an allergic reaction.

45
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:48,000
An extreme allergic reaction
is known as anaphylactic shock.

46
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Depending on the circumstances,

47
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:51,000
it can be fatal.

48
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:54,000
That’s what happened. You got me.

49
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,000
So, you killed him with bees?

50
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Bourbon was who I drew as my target.

51
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:11,000
Once I’d confirmed he was inside the cave,

52
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:14,000
I sprayed sleeping gas into the entrance

53
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:17,000
then waited until it was safe to go in.

54
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:32,000
When I found him,

55
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:34,000
Bourbon was completely passed out.

56
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:36,000
But he had already set up his traps.

57
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,000
[Ponzu screaming]

58
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:41,000
And unfortunately for me,

59
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:45,000
there were snakes in the back of the cave,
hiding in crevices.

60
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:47,000
I guess the sleeping gas
didn’t reach them.

61
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:51,000
I was able to jump out of the way
just in the nick of time,

62
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:54,000
so I didn’t get bitten by them
or anything.

63
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:57,000
But that’s what triggered my own defenses
to activate.

64
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,000
[gasps]

65
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:04,000
That’s where you keep all your bees?

66
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,000
[buzzing]

67
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:08,000
If I scream, collapse,
or anything like that,

68
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:11,000
these little guys
will attack anyone nearby.

69
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:14,000
I wasn’t expecting him to die, though.

70
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:18,000
How could I have known
he was allergic to bees?

71
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:21,000
And the snakes kept me from helping him.

72
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:24,000
Well not like I could’ve done anything.

73
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:27,000
You can come back now.

74
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,000
The problem is the person
who set the trap in the first place

75
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:37,000
died without ever having the chance
to deactivate it.

76
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:41,000
And we can’t exactly disarm it
or ask him for help.

77
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:44,000
We’re trapped with no hope for escape.

78
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:46,000
[Leorio groans]

79
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:47,000
Leorio.

80
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:49,000
[sighs]

81
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:51,000
So, it’s hopeless. I gave up.

82
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:55,000
We’re stuck until the Exam Committee
comes and saves us.

83
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:56,000
The Exam Committee?

84
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:59,000
Are you saying they’ll rescue us
from this cave?

85
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:01,000
You didn’t know?

86
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:05,000
Each of our number badges
contain transmitters.

87
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:09,000
The Examiners know where all
the applicants are located at all times,

88
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:11,000
and if someone hasn’t returned
by the deadline,

89
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:13,000
they go out and look for them.

90
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:17,000
However, if it’s lost or stolen,
then you’re on your own.

91
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,000
Luckily, there’s only one more day left.

92
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:23,000
Best to just give up for this year
and wait for help.

93
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:25,000
We can’t do that.

94
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:28,000
Leorio’s condition is worsening.

95
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:30,000
He needs to get to a doctor.

96
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:34,000
The Examiners aren’t going to budge
‘til it’s past the deadline.

97
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:37,000
If you don’t have your badge,
you’ll be left for dead.

98
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:41,000
This is his fault, really.

99
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:42,000
I tried to warn him.

100
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:46,000
Kurapika! Gon! Don’t come in here!!

101
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:50,000
[screaming]

102
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:52,000
All you can do for him

103
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:55,000
is pray that he can manage to hang on
until help can arrive.

104
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:57,000
No.

105
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:58,000
There’s another way.

106
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:01,000
One with a good chance of success.

107
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:03,000
But if he isn’t carrying any,

108
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:06,000
we’ll have another fatality on our hands.

109
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,000
[Gon] Kurapika.

110
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,000
-Take care of Leorio.
-But Gon...

111
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:13,000
It’s there. Don’t worry.

112
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,000
Gon…

113
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:17,000
Gon! Hey!

114
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:21,000
Are you crazy? What are you doing?

115
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:23,000
Didn’t you hear a word I just said?

116
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:24,000
[gulps]

117
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:27,000
[hissing]

118
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:31,000
[screams]

119
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:35,000
[grunting]

120
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:36,000
Oh, no!

121
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:39,000
He-- he’s out of his mind!

122
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,000
[straining]

123
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:47,000
[Gon] Found it!

124
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,000
[both gasp]

125
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:50,000
[Gon] Kurapika! Catch!

126
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:53,000
Gon!

127
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:04,000
Hurry! Give it... to Leorio!

128
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:17,000
There. You ready, Gon?

129
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,000
Yeah…

130
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:20,000
I don’t believe it.

131
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:24,000
He jumped into a nest of snakes
looking for an antidote

132
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:26,000
he wasn’t sure was there!

133
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,000
[Kurapika]
True, but the odds were in his favor.

134
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,000
If you poison someone,

135
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:35,000
you can’t bargain
unless you have the antidote.

136
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:37,000
Yeah, but it was still pretty risky.

137
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,000
[Kurapika] That said...

138
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,000
doing what Gon just did

139
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:43,000
took an incredible amount of courage.

140
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:48,000
He’s stabilizing.

141
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:50,000
He should be all right.

142
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:52,000
You must be really good friends.

143
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:58,000
Hey! Do you have
any of your sleeping gas left over?

144
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:00,000
I do.

145
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:02,000
Will you trade it for this?

146
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:05,000
That’s Bourbon’s badge!

147
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:06,000
And if you had it,

148
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:08,000
it would give you the six points you need.

149
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:10,000
Yeah. That’s right.

150
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:13,000
But, uh… What are you planning
to do with it?

151
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:14,000
The sleeping gas?

152
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:15,000
Use it!

153
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:18,000
We’ll put all the snakes to sleep,
then we can escape.

154
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:19,000
Releasing it in here

155
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:23,000
would be much more effective
than when I used it at the entrance.

156
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:26,000
Within five minutes,
the cave will fill with gas,

157
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:28,000
knocking all the snakes out cold.

158
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:30,000
That’s five whole minutes!

159
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:33,000
Which is way longer
than anyone can hold their breath!

160
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,000
I mean, what’s the point in trying

161
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:37,000
if we’re all just going
to put ourselves to sleep in the process?

162
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:39,000
Nine minutes and 44 seconds.

163
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,000
What?

164
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:42,000
My record for holding my breath.

165
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,000
You can count on me.

166
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:46,000
I’ll carry you out of here.

167
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:49,000
Why should I trust you?

168
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:52,000
You’re just gonna leave me here
and escape by yourself.

169
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:53,000
You believe that?

170
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:55,000
You saw what he did.

171
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:57,000
Gon braved a nest of venomous snakes

172
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:58,000
to save Leorio.

173
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,000
[Gon] Trust me.

174
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:03,000
I’ll get you out.

175
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:04,000
I promise I will.

176
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:15,000
It’s ready to go.

177
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:18,000
[Gon] Wait for my signal,
then release the gas.

178
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:19,000
Ready and waiting.

179
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,000
[exhales]

180
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:24,000
[takes a deep inhale and holds breath]

181
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:33,000
[exhales]

182
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:35,000
[inhales and passes out]

183
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:37,000
[Gon] 199.

184
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:39,000
200.

185
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:40,000
201.

186
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:41,000
202.

187
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:43,000
203.

188
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:44,000
204.

189
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:46,000
205. [Gon's voice fading out]

190
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,000
206.

191
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:48,000
207.

192
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:01,000
[big exhale]

193
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:03,000
[Gon] All right!

194
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:15,000
Well I’ll leave Bourbon’s badge
here with you.

195
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:17,000
So, the Committee can find you.

196
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:22,000
Yours goes to Leorio.

197
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:25,000
That way, he’ll have his six points
and he can pass.

198
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:28,000
Consider it a small fee for saving you.

199
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:30,000
Sorry about that!

200
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:38,000
[Khara] Phase Four of the Hunter Exam
is now officially over!

201
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:40,000
All remaining applicants,

202
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:43,000
please return to the starting point
at once!

203
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:48,000
You will be given one additional hour
to make your way back.

204
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:51,000
If you still haven’t returned
by the time that hour is up,

205
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:53,000
you will fail the Exam.

206
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:58,000
Furthermore, exchanging badges
at the starting point is prohibited.

207
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:03,000
Any attempt to do so
will result in immediate disqualification.

208
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:10,000
HUNTER GLOSSARY

209
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:15,000
PONZU

210
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:21,000
[trumpets playing fanfare]

211
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:25,000
Now we will check the badges
of everyone present here.

212
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:29,000
Number 44, Mr. Hisoka.

213
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:32,000
Number 58, Mr. Pokkle.

214
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:35,000
Number 99, Mr. Killua.

215
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:38,000
Number 301, Mr. Gittarackur.

216
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:41,000
Number 191, Mr. Bodoro.

217
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,000
Number 294, Mr. Hanzo.

218
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:48,000
So only six applicants have passed?

219
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:49,000
Oh, wait!

220
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:51,000
Hm?

221
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:55,000
Gon!

222
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:57,000
Three more!

223
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:59,000
You’re certainly cutting it close,
aren’t you?

224
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:00,000
Killua.

225
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:06,000
[smirks]

226
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:11,000
Now the last three!

227
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:12,000
They are…

228
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:15,000
Number 404, Mr. Kurapika.

229
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:18,000
Number 403, Mr. Leorio.

230
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:22,000
And Number 405, Mr. Gon.

231
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:28,000
So, these nine applicants have passed
the Fourth Phase of the Exam!

232
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:32,000
[Netero laughing]

233
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:35,000
Six of the nine that have passed
are rookies?

234
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:37,000
Marvelous, marvelous!

235
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:40,000
Has that ever happened before?

236
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:43,000
Ah. Well, there has been a trend lately.

237
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:46,000
We’ll sometimes
go several years in a row

238
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:48,000
without a single rookie
worthy of qualifying.

239
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:53,000
And then we’ll suddenly have
a whole bunch of promising newbies apply.

240
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:57,000
This makes four times
since I became Chairman.

241
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,000
By the way, sir,

242
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:01,000
what will we be doing for the Final Phase?

243
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:03,000
Oh yeah, that’s right!

244
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:05,000
You haven’t told us
what you have planned yet!

245
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:08,000
Ah, yes. Well, about that…

246
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:11,000
They’ll be participating
in a rather peculiar fight.

247
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:12,000
Hm?

248
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:14,000
A “peculiar fight”, you say?

249
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:17,000
Gather the nine remaining applicants.

250
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:20,000
I’d like to speak with each of them alone.

251
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:26,000
Dammit, I’m so pathetic.

252
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:28,000
The whole Fourth Phase...

253
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:31,000
I relied on you two
to do everything for me.

254
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,000
I promise I’ll return the favor.

255
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:35,000
So...

256
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:38,000
uh, well, thanks, you guys.

257
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:41,000
[Beans over speaker]
Attention, all applicants.

258
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:44,000
The Chairman wishes to interview you.

259
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:45,000
Really?

260
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:47,000
[Beans] When you hear your number,

261
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:49,000
come to the reception room
on the second floor.

262
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:53,000
We’ll start with number 44, Mr. Hisoka.

263
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:55,000
Thank you for your cooperation.

264
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:04,000
Please, make yourself comfortable.

265
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:07,000
Don’t tell me
that this is the Final Phase?

266
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:10,000
Not the test itself, you understand.

267
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:12,000
I just have a few questions,

268
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:15,000
mostly to satisfy my own curiosity.

269
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:17,000
Hmm...

270
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,000
To start with,

271
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:24,000
why do you want to become a Hunter?

272
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:26,000
[Hisoka] To be frank, I don’t. But...

273
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:28,000
Go on.

274
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:31,000
A Hunter License can be incredibly useful.

275
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:33,000
[Netero] Oh. And how so?

276
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:34,000
For example,

277
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:39,000
Hunters can often kill
without any fear of prosecution.

278
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:41,000
I understand.

279
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:43,000
Moving on to the next question…

280
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:46,000
Out of the other eight applicants,

281
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:48,000
which one are you keeping a close eye on?

282
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:52,000
Number 99.

283
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:53,000
Ooh.

284
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:56,000
405 also caught my eye,

285
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:58,000
but not like 99.

286
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,000
I would love to challenge him one day.

287
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:02,000
[chuckling]

288
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:05,000
Well, one last question and we’re done.

289
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:08,000
Which of the other
eight remaining applicants

290
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:09,000
would you least want to fight?

291
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:13,000
That would be number 405.

292
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:16,000
Though 99 is a close second.

293
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:17,000
[Netero] Ah...

294
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:19,000
[Hisoka] The time simply isn’t right.

295
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:22,000
As for now, I’d have to say number 405.

296
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:24,000
Hm... Understood.

297
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:29,000
However, the one I would
most like to fight right now...

298
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:32,000
would have to be you.

299
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:35,000
Well. Thank you very much.

300
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:37,000
That’ll be all.

301
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:45,000
That is one sly old man.

302
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:52,000
He left himself so open
that I lost my edge.

303
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:00,000
I’m keeping an eye focused on Number 404.

304
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:02,000
He’s the most well-rounded applicant.

305
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:06,000
But I don’t want to fight with 44.

306
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:09,000
Because... I don’t think I could beat him.

307
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:13,000
Well, Gon. We’re the same age.

308
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:17,000
Who I don’t wanna fight,
though is number 53.

309
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:19,000
I don’t think it’d be very fun at all.

310
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:24,000
I'm keeping my eye on Number 44.

311
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:26,000
You can't help but notice him.

312
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:29,000
Numbers 405 and 99 are out, however.

313
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:32,000
I simply will not fight children.

314
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:38,000
Number 99.

315
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:39,000
[clacking]

316
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:41,000
And Number 44.

317
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:45,000
Who am I keeping an eye on?

318
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:47,000
Hisoka, Number 44.

319
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:49,000
He’s on my mind the most, anyway.

320
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:53,000
But there’s no way
I could ever pick Number 99,

321
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:56,000
Number 403 or Number 404.

322
00:17:58,000 --> 00:17:59,000
It has to be 44.

323
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:02,000
He’s obviously
the most dangerous applicant.

324
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:07,000
The one I’d least want to meet in combat
is also 44.

325
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:10,000
I’m watching 405,

326
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:12,000
purely for positive reasons.

327
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,000
44 for negative reasons.

328
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:17,000
I will fight anyone if there’s a reason.

329
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:20,000
Otherwise I’d rather not fight at all.

330
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:23,000
Number 405.

331
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:26,000
I owe him and I sure hope he passes.

332
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:30,000
That’s why he’s the one
I really don’t want to fight.

333
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:33,000
Hm, I see.

334
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:35,000
This is more lopsided than I expected.

335
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:45,000
-Gon.
-Huh?

336
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:47,000
So, we made it to the Final Phase.

337
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:54,000
HEART-SPIRIT

338
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:56,000
Hm. That'll do it.

339
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:03,000
Sorry to keep you all waiting.

340
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:05,000
I’ve drawn up the brackets.

341
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:07,000
-Huh?
-What’s this?

342
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:10,000
But-- But Chairman!

343
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:13,000
Come on! You can’t be serious!

344
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:15,000
[laughing]

345
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:18,000
Oh, I am quite serious.

346
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:21,000
That look. He’s serious indeed.

347
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:24,000
That’s a serious look? You sure?

348
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:28,000
The winners will pass the Exam
and earn the title of Hunter.

349
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:34,000
Gon.

350
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:41,000
Did something happen in the Fourth Phase?

351
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:45,000
Since we met up...

352
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:48,000
you’ve been acting strangely
and I’m getting concerned.

353
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:51,000
Ever since we left Zevil Island,

354
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:53,000
you’ve seemed rather quiet.

355
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:55,000
[Gon] My target...

356
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:57,000
was Hisoka.

357
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:02,000
I waited for the perfect chance
and stole his badge.

358
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:06,000
But someone else was following me

359
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:09,000
and he got me with a poison dart.

360
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:14,000
After that, Hisoka showed up

361
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:16,000
and took his badge
from the guy who took it from me

362
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:18,000
and then left it.

363
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:21,000
He said I owed him now.

364
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:22,000
He really said that?

365
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:24,000
[Gon] I said I didn’t need it

366
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:26,000
and he sent me flying.

367
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:33,000
[Hisoka] I will take it back

368
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:36,000
but only when you can
punch me in the face like that.

369
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:42,000
[Gon] I was just so mad at myself.

370
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:44,000
I couldn’t do anything.

371
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:47,000
I was helpless against him.

372
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:05,000
And when he left,

373
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:07,000
I got so miserable and lonely.

374
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:08,000
It was just awful.

375
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:11,000
I guess it hurt to realize

376
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:13,000
that I wasn’t strong enough
to challenge him.

377
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:15,000
That’s why I wanted some company.

378
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:18,000
I wanted to find somebody
I could help.

379
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:20,000
I guess.

380
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:24,000
That’s when I decided
to look for the two of you.

381
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:25,000
Gon...

382
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:28,000
Without your assistance,

383
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:31,000
Leorio and I
never would have made it this far.

384
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:34,000
Thank you.

385
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:35,000
For everything.

386
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:39,000
I feel the same way.

387
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:41,000
Thank you, too.

388
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:49,000
[narrator]
Gon and his friends have grown closer.

389
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:52,000
And the nine remaining applicants

390
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:55,000
are about to enter the Exam’s Final Phase.

391
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:00,000
[theme song playing]

392
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:26,000
[Gon] Next time:
"Can't Win x And x Can't Lose"!

393
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:28,000
[Killua] Then how do I win?

394
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:29,000
[Gon] Give it all you’ve got!
